Even with the standard deduction, you can claim "above-the-line" adjustments to income and business deductions for your freelance work:

*   **Student Loan Interest:** You paid $4,400, but the IRS caps the student loan interest deduction at **$2,500** per return. Based on your combined income, you are well below the phase-out limit, so you can deduct the full $2,500.
*   **Home Office Deduction (for your 1099 work):** Because you use the 155 sq ft space *exclusively* for your freelance business, you can deduct it against your $14,600 in 1099 income. You have two ways to calculate this:
